  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 135 AM EDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nA drier Saharan Air Layer moves in Tuesday into Wednesday as the \nridge axis slides a bit further north along the peninsula of \nFlorida. This will allow for the easterly to southeasterly wind flow \nto persist while the lower relative atmospheric moisture will \nprovide lower convective coverage focused inland in the afternoons. \nThe dry air will linger until late in the week when the next burst \nof tropical moisture begins to arrive from the Bahamas and Greater \nAntilles Friday into Saturday to close out the week. This moisture \nwill allow convective activity to trend closer to seasonal norms \nbased on the current forecast guidance.\n\nGiven the relative decrease in showers and storms forecast for a \ngood portion of the long term forecast period, temperatures will \nbegin a warming trend with lower to mid 90s becoming the story \nacross much of the area. Triple digit heat index values are forecast \nand the potential for Heat Advisories will need to be monitored day-\nto-day, particularly over the urbanized areas.",
